#
# Rows for scripts/bench-poses.sh. Whitespace-separated columns; '-' = none;
# paths relative to the repo root and may use $VARIABLES (a row whose
# variable is unset is skipped). `configs` is a comma-separated list from
# {none, optimize, manhattan, register, opt-register, xfeat}; each produces
# one report row named "<name>:<config>". `xfeat` is accepted but currently
# always skipped -- no XFeat loop-closure front end is wired into `rux
# graph discover` yet (docs/research/visual-drift-loop.md references the
# matcher as research-branch only); remove it from a row once reusex-rcv.1.9
# or a successor lands it.
#
# name              kind       project                                       reference  configs
#
# office_corridor (committed fixture, sensor frames only, no drift of its
# own): the script perturbs a COPY with a fixed seed and scores every config
# against the UNPERTURBED copy's own trajectory as a placeholder reference
# (kind=synthetic), proving the mechanics (reference export, perturbation,
# per-config run, report shape) end to end with no external data. It is only
# 10 frames, too sparse for `rux optimize` to find landmarks after drift is
# injected (it correctly warns and leaves poses unchanged, so 'none' and
# 'optimize' score identically here) -- a real "worse vs better" demonstration
# needs a scan with enough structure, e.g. an ARKitScenes copy perturbed the
# same way (verified manually for reusex-rcv.1.6; not committed, see
# scripts/bench-arkitscenes-drift.sh for that dataset's own harness).
office_corridor    synthetic  tests/fixtures/scans/office_corridor.rux      -          none,optimize,manhattan
# Local-only rows (never committed data), skipped unless the variable is set.
# A pose reference is authored with the drift-correction loop (reusex-rcv.1.8)
# and committed under tests/fixtures/pose_reference/<scan>.trajectory.tum.
house1             local      $REUSEX_HOUSE1_RUX                            tests/fixtures/pose_reference/house1.trajectory.tum    none,optimize,manhattan,register,opt-register
house2             local      $REUSEX_HOUSE2_RUX                            tests/fixtures/pose_reference/house2.trajectory.tum    none,optimize,manhattan,register,opt-register
